{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>When the place is far off, etc.</b> It comes to permit what was forbidden in the wilderness — to eat outside of sacrificial offerings of shelamim. And He stated the reason for the permit in the pleasantness of His words, saying ״כִּי יִרְחַק״ (when it is far). Therefore He said, <b>and you shall eat within your gates</b>, and there is no need to bring it to the Sanctuary. And the meaning of ״יִרְחַק״ is: anyone who stands in a distant place. And we find that our Sages of blessed memory (Pesachim 93b) disagreed concerning the verse ״וּבְדֶרֶךְ רְחוֹקָה״: some say from Modi'im and outward, and some say from the entrance of Jerusalem, and some say from the entrance of the Azarah. And it is possible to say: every person who slaughters at the entrance of the Azarah an animal from which they would offer a sacrifice to HaShem — which he may not slaughter except as shelamim to HaShem — when would this verse apply to him so that I may fulfill it?"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:54.104775502Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}